//! with C names and C layout: the Rust "header" of the C API. GENERATED by
//! a generator from the headers - regenerate, do not edit this file by hand.
//!
//! Standard library only and engine-free: extension crates (`duckdb-ext-api`) depend on it alone, so an
//! extension built as a cdylib carries no engine code and talks to the engine that loaded it through the
//! `duckdb_ext_api_v2` function table.
//!
//! Enums are `#[repr(transparent)]` newtypes over `c_int` (the C enums pin their underlying
//! type to `int` through a `0x7FFFFFFF` member) with the members as associated free constants,
//! so unknown values coming from C are representable. Handles are pointers to one-field structs
//! exactly as in C; the pointee is never dereferenced, the engine casts the pointer to its own
//! handle type.
